--TEST--
`Core\Response\Stream::end` on a stream with a length ends it before the length is reached, and every later write throws, an empty one included — `rule:core-classes/spreadsheet-writes-as-a-stream`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Response\Stream::end
// Two of the five bytes are written, and then the body is ended. The window still
// says five, and a write of the rest throws because the stream has ended.
var $body = Core\Response::stream("text/plain; charset=utf-8", 5);
$body->write("He");
$body->end();
array<string> $rests = ["llo", ""];
foreach ($rests as string $rest) {
    try {
        $body->write($rest);
    } catch (LogicError $error) {
        echo "\n", $error->message;
    }
}
echo "\n", $body->length(), "\n";
--EXPECT--
He
Core\Response\Stream::write(): the stream has ended, because `end()` was called. Nothing was sent.
Core\Response\Stream::write(): the stream has ended, because `end()` was called. Nothing was sent.
5
